# Accepted security advisories for the backend pip-audit gate.
#
# Read by scripts/pip_audit_gate.py. One row per advisory:
#
#     <ID>  <review-by>  <owner>  <why accepting this is safe>
#
# `review-by` is a deadline, not a note: once it passes, the gate fails and the
# row must be re-assessed. Keep `why` falsifiable — name the code fact that makes
# the advisory unreachable, not an opinion. Delete rows pip-audit stops
# reporting; the gate prints those as stale.
#
# Scope note: every row below belongs to the GPU stack that now lives in
# gpu-worker/requirements.txt (the old backend/requirements.txt was deleted with
# the 2026-10 split). The public server installs requirements-cloud.txt, which
# carries no suppressions — torch/transformers/nltk are not in it, and its web
# stack (fastapi/starlette/sentry-sdk) sits on fixed versions. This gate audits
# requirements-cloud.txt only, so these rows can never be matched here.
#
# ⚠️ The GPU worker's own gate reads gpu-worker/.pip-audit-ignore, NOT this file.
# Keeping a second copy here means two lists drift (they already have: this one
# lacks PYSEC-2026-4174 and holds CVE-2026-80047 / PYSEC-2026-3740, which the GPU
# list does not). Rows here are kept only as the historical record while the
# stale-warning is a known, harmless noise source; treat
# gpu-worker/.pip-audit-ignore as the live list.
#
# Re-assessed 2026-09-19: none of these are fixable by a version bump we can land
# safely today. The torch and transformers fixes are GPU-stack major upgrades —
# torch is pinned in lockstep with torchaudio/torchvision CUDA builds and
# pyannote-audio — which belong in their own change, not in a scanner-driven bump.
#
# Re-assessed 2026-10-02: CVE-2026-80047 added (new disclosure against the
# unchanged transformers, CI red on master). Upstream has published no fix at all
# (GitLab advisory: "no solution available yet"; affected 4.49.0–5.8.1), so a bump
# is not an option — the row records why the entry point is unreachable instead.

# ── torch: the 8 advisories all target operator/deserialization paths we do not call ──
PYSEC-2025-193  2027-03-01  backend  torch.nn.utils.rnn.unpack_sequence 内存破坏。公告的 last_affected 写作 "2.6.0-NA"（非法版本号），OSV 据此判 2.8.0 不在范围内、pip-audit 判在范围内——按公告本体我们本就出界；且需本地访问（AV:L），app/ 只用 torch.cuda.*
PYSEC-2025-194  2027-03-01  backend  torch.jit.script 内存破坏，同样本地攻击面、同样受 "2.6.0-NA" 边界影响；项目任何地方都不使用 TorchScript
PYSEC-2025-195  2027-03-01  backend  torch.lstm_cell 内存破坏，同样本地攻击面、同样受 "2.6.0-NA" 边界影响；项目不调用该算子，RNN 由 ctranslate2 以自有实现执行
PYSEC-2025-203  2027-03-01  backend  torch.linalg.lu 切片 DoS，需攻击者控制送入该算子的张量；项目无任何 linalg.lu 调用路径
PYSEC-2025-204  2027-03-01  backend  torch.rot90 + torch.randn_like 组合异常，需攻击者控制张量；项目无这两个算子的调用路径
PYSEC-2025-206  2027-03-01  backend  torch.nan_to_num().long() 整数溢出，需攻击者控制张量；项目无该调用路径
PYSEC-2026-139  2027-03-01  backend  pt2 加载处理器反序列化，公告标注仅本地可利用；项目不加载 .pt2 产物
PYSEC-2026-2286  2027-03-01  backend  恶意 .pth 即使经 torch.load(weights_only=True) 也能内存破坏（修复于 2.10.0）；app/ 无 torch.load 调用，模型产物来自固定仓库名

# ── transformers: all 6 require loading an attacker-controlled model repo or checkpoint ──
PYSEC-2025-217  2027-03-01  backend  X-CLIP checkpoint 转换反序列化，需受害者打开恶意文件；项目不加载 X-CLIP，且无 checkpoint 转换路径
PYSEC-2026-2288  2027-03-01  backend  Trainer._load_rng_state 未加 weights_only；项目不使用 Trainer，且 torch 2.8（>=2.6）已使 safe_globals 生效
PYSEC-2026-2289  2027-03-01  backend  恶意 config.json 的 _attn_implementation_internal 触发远端代码执行；项目不调用 AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained，也不接受用户提供的模型仓库
PYSEC-2026-2290  2027-03-01  backend  LightGlue 加载路径下 trust_remote_code 被 config.json 覆盖；项目不加载 LightGlue，全仓无 trust_remote_code 调用
PYSEC-2026-3929  2027-03-01  backend  save_pretrained 经 chat template 名做路径穿越；项目只做推理，全仓无 save_pretrained 调用
CVE-2026-80047  2027-03-01  backend  load_custom_generate() 在 trust_remote_code 同意之前就把 custom_generate/generate.py 写进 ~/.cache/huggingface/modules（GitLab: 4.49.0–5.8.1，无修复版本；CVSS 向量 AV:L）。全仓无 load_custom_generate 调用、无 trust_remote_code，模型仓库全是固定名（whisperx "auto" 对齐模型、oliverguhr 标点模型），不接受用户提供的仓库或 checkpoint——写盘必须先有一次我们不会发起的调用

